{"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/accepting(_:)","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/droppingCallSite()","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/redactingSensitiveValues()"],"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"Where a delivery sends events: a plain sink that records the batches it receives.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Destination","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:)"},{"type":"text","text":" gives each destination its batches in the order the events"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"were tracked, one at a time: the next batch comes once "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" returns. Batches that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arrive meanwhile wait in a buffer of the destination’s own, which drops its oldest batch when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"full, so a destination that falls behind loses batches rather than holding up the others."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" should return promptly and honour cancellation: a delivery waits for it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before it completes, and cancels it when the delivery is cancelled. A destination handles its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own errors (a failed upload, say); the delivery has none to receive."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When a tracker keeps its records in a store, returning from "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is what tells the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store a batch arrived: once every destination has returned for it, uncancelled, the store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"forgets those records. A destination that buffers or retries should return only once the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch is somewhere it won’t be lost; a record whose "},{"code":"EventRecord.isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is set may"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"have reached it in an earlier run."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What a destination receives is narrowed by modifiers rather than by code of its own:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/accepting(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" for the consent categories it serves, "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/redactingSensitiveValues()"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/droppingCallSite()"},{"type":"text","text":". A destination given none receives every record as tracked."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/destinations\/destination"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Destinations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"inheritsFrom","title":"Inherits From"},{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/ConsoleDestination","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination"],"type":"conformingTypes","title":"Conforming Types"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"protocol","modules":[{"name":"Destinations"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Destination.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Destinations\/Destination.swift#L23"},"role":"symbol","title":"Destination","roleHeading":"Protocol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Destination","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Destination","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:12Destinations11DestinationP"},"references":{"doc://Destinations/documentation/Destinations/Destination/receive(_:)":{"title":"receive(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/destinations\/destination\/receive(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"receive","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"([","kind":"text"},{"text":"EventRecord","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events11EventRecordV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Records "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"